From: JorreFog <JorreFog@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake config: exec_prefix relative to the found prefix

sdl2_ttf-config.cmake works out prefix from its own location, so it can
be used from a sysroot, but took exec_prefix from configure. Configured
with --exec-prefix=/usr (as Buildroot does), libdir became the build
machine's /usr/lib, and a cross build that found SDL2_ttf through this
file linked /usr/lib/libSDL2_ttf.so of the build machine ("file in wrong
format"). The CMake build of SDL2_ttf already writes ${prefix} here.

--- a/sdl2_ttf-config.cmake.in
+++ b/sdl2_ttf-config.cmake.in
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 
 get_filename_component(CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR ${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR} REALPATH)
 get_filename_component(prefix "${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/@cmake_prefix_relpath@" ABSOLUTE)
-set(exec_prefix "@exec_prefix@")
+set(exec_prefix "${prefix}")
 set(bindir "@bindir@")
 set(includedir "@includedir@")
 set(libdir "@libdir@")
